<Page
  title="Privacy"
  description="What teamtoolbox does and doesn't collect, in plain language."
  draft
>
  <p>
    <strong>In short:</strong> we can't read what you put into teamtoolbox, there are no accounts,
    and the tools use no cookies or tracking.
  </p>

  <h2>What you put into the tools</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Tools that stay in your browser</strong> store what you enter on your device only. It
      never reaches us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Shared tools</strong> encrypt what you enter in your browser before sending it. We
      store only encrypted data we can't read, in the EU, and delete it when the room expires (at
      most 90 days after it's created) or when someone in the room wipes it.
      <a href="/security">How the encryption works</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Technical data</h2>
  <p>
    Like any website, our host (Cloudflare) processes your IP address and browser details to deliver
    pages and to stop abuse. We don't log or store them. Rate limits that protect the service are
    kept in memory only.
  </p>

  <h2>Ads</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>In the tools:</strong> each tool shows one small ad that our own code displays. We
      count how often each ad is shown and clicked, in total, with no identifiers. When an ad comes
      from an ad network, your browser loads its image from that network, which then sees your IP
      address and browser details. No ad can see what you've entered.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>On teamtoolbox.org:</strong> we may show Google AdSense ads. If we do, they'll only
      appear on the directory pages, and visitors from the EU, UK and Switzerland will be asked for
      consent first.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The tools set no cookies. The directory site sets none either, unless ads are enabled there and
    you consent to them.
  </p>

  <h2>Who processes data for us</h2>
  <p>Cloudflare, Inc. hosts the site and stores the encrypted rooms.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because we don't know who you are and can't read room contents, there's usually nothing we can
    link to you. You can delete shared rooms yourself at any time. For any other question, contact
    us via the details on our <a href="/about">about page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, we'll update this page. The full history is visible in our public
    repository.
  </p>
</Page>
